{"seq":17,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-safety-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:25:58.300Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"15d3f765cca34f0d0ab69c5d4e8fce22d2ddc4b2eb9004c760e3754a6ce410f2","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Doors 14–18 in Eau Claire weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct. There was also a follow-up item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also logged by Thea. Gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for firmware testing.\n\nWhat I left out:\n• The 9/14/2025 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal note mention QFL, but neither has a ticket number.\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central notes are for Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company. It isn't a customer.\n\nMoss's notes don't give a status for #4419 after the escalation, so you may want to check whether it's still open before it goes in the weekly notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
